[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: TC-H1FWMC-
TITLE: Test Protocol

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-88
TITLE: Discharge 2
STATEMENT: >>>
Warm the system into "Staged" status and leave the system running without intervention for 5 minutes. Ensure that the system returns to cold state.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to use
2. The treatment plan is already loaded
3. Launch a timer to set the time
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Prepare button
2. Check system's status
3. Start the timer
4. Wait for 5 minutes
5. Check system's status
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the prepare button is clicked and the proper message is displaying in the GUI
2. Verify system switches to "Staged" status (check the top section of the monitor to find the status)
3. Verify 5 minutes passed
4. Verify system goes to COLD status
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-87
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-89
TITLE: Operation 11: Termination
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user starts the emission and presses the stop button, make sure the emission terminated.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to use and runs an emission
2. Treatment plan is loaded and ready to run and emission
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start running the treatment plan and start the emission
2. Click the Stop button in the middle of emission
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the plan started to run and the emission is started
2. Verify the emission is terminated
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-1
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-90
TITLE: Head Interface 1
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user presses and releases keys in the keypad of the head of the system, the service screen should record all of the toggles.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Press and release keys in the keypad of the head in the system
2. Click the Services symbol in the left panel of the screen
3. Check the services
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the toggles of the keys that happened and record all of the toggles accordingly
2. Verify services screen is displayed in the GUI
3. Verify all of the keypad toggles are displayed and recorded in the services screen
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-2
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-91
TITLE: Head Interface 2
STATEMENT: >>>
When the head interface board is unplugged from main control board, a fault should display in the system after 3 seconds.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run
2. Treatment plan is uploaded and ready to run
3. Head interface board is plugged into the main control board
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Unplug the head interface board from main board
2. Check the fault after 3 seconds
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify physically that the head interface is unplugged from main board
2. Verify fault is displayed for unplugged head interface board
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-3
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-92
TITLE: Fault Information 1
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user stops the system during run time, a fault will happen on GUI and the details of the fault can be seen in logs.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is on and running
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. When the system is running, push the e-stop button
2. Click the Logs symbol in the left panel of the screen
3. Check the faults on the log screen
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system induces a fault and the status displays a fault status in the GUI
2. Verify logs are displayed in the middle of the screen
3. Verify the fault was logged with the type, state, expected and measured details
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-6
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-93
TITLE: Emission Indicator
STATEMENT: >>>
The user can hear sounds during the emission which is provided by the audible indicator in the main board.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. Emission is running
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. When an emission is running, check the sound
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the user can hear the sound which is enabled by firmware and can be heard because of the audible indicator in the main board
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-7
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-94
TITLE: Interlocks
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall monitor the status of the interlocks and throw a fault if any unusual things happen.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is on and ready to run
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Press and release the e-stop button in the system
2. Click Services symbol in the left panel of the screen
3. Check the services
4. Change the state of Ion pump HV interlocks
5. Click Services symbol in the left panel of the screen
6. Check the services
7. Change the state of KUKA robot arm interlocks
8. Click Services symbol in the left panel of the screen
9. Check the services
10. Change the state of Door interlock
11. Click Services symbol in the left panel of the screen
12. Check the services
13. Change the state of Coolant level sensor
14. Click Services symbol in the left panel of the screen
15. Check the services
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the toggles of the e-stop button happened
2. Verify services screen is displayed in the GUI
3. Verify the e-stop toggle is recorded in the services screen after 1 second
4. Verify Ion pump HV interlocks status changed
5. Verify services screen is displayed in the GUI
6. Verify Ion pump HV interlocks status is recorded in the services screen
7. Verify KUKA robot arm interlocks status changed
8. Verify services screen is displayed in the GUI
9. Verify KUKA robot arm interlocks status is recorded in the services screen
10. Verify Door interlock status changed
11. Verify services screen is displayed in the GUI
12. Verify Door interlock status is recorded in the services screen
13. Verify Coolant level sensor status changed
14. Verify services screen is displayed in the GUI
15. Verify Coolant level sensor status is recorded in the services screen
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-8
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-95
TITLE: Coils 1
STATEMENT: >>>
When an emission starts to run after the Focus Coil is unplugged, a fault can be found in the logs.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run an emission
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Unplug the Focus Coil
2. Run an emission
3. Click the Log symbol in the left panel of the screen
4. Check the log
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify physically that the Focus Coil is unplugged
2. Verify the emission started
3. Verify logs are displayed in the middle of the screen
4. Verify there are faults displayed in the log for values that are more than 150 mA out of tolerance
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-9
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-96
TITLE: Backup Timer 1
STATEMENT: >>>
Load test version of timer firmware to simulate corrupted communication. Run system and look for timer fault in log.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The test version of timer firmware to simulate corrupted communication is loaded
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Restart the system
2. Click the Log button at the left-hand side of the monitor
3. Look for timer fault in log and verify it's corrupted
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system is ready to operate and use
2. Verify the logs are displayed in the screen
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-10
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-97
TITLE: Backup Timer 2
STATEMENT: >>>
Delete timer firmware to simulate lack of communication. Run system and look for timer fault in log.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. Timer firmware is deleted
2. System is in Ready status
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Restart the system
2. Start the timer
3. Click the Log button at the left-hand side of the monitor
4. Look for fault in log and verify it's reported after TBD seconds
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system is ready to operate and use
2. Verify it started from 0
3. Verify the logs are displayed in the screen
4. Verify the related fault is displayed in the log after TBD seconds
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-11
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-98
TITLE: Operation 01: Filament Conditioning 6
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall report a fault if the HVPS has not reached the target filament current setpoint during the conditioning procedure within a timeout period of 20 minutes.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. HVPS firmware must have a filament limit of 1500 mA
2. System is ready to run
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Load specialized HVPS interface firmware
2. Start up the system
3. Create filament conditioning
4. Wait for some time
5. Check the fault
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the current of filament is 1500 mA
2. Verify the system is started
3. Verify the filament's conditioning is started
4. Wait for 20 minutes +/- 10 seconds
5. Verify a fault is triggered
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-12
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-99
TITLE: Operation 02: Warmup Procedure
STATEMENT: >>>
When user loads a firmware that reports a fault if the HVPS interface has a filament current limit of 1500 mA during the conditioning procedure within a timeout period of 30 minutes +/- 2 seconds.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. HVPS firmware must have a filament limit of 1500 mA
2. System is ready to run
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Load specialized HVPS interface firmware
2. Start up the system
3. Create filament conditioning
4. Start the Warmup
5. Wait for some time
6. Check the fault
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the current of filament current is limited to 1500 mA
2. Verify the system is started
3. Verify the filament's conditioning is started
4. Verify Warmup is started
5. Wait for 30 minutes +/- 2 seconds
6. Verify a fault is triggered
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-13
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-100
TITLE: Operation 07: Operational Point Setup
STATEMENT: >>>
When the high voltage interlock jumper is removed from the HVPS, verify that the system creates a fault.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is up and ready to run
2. The high voltage interlock jumper is removed from the HVPS
3. A treatment plan is ready to load and run
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Remove the high voltage interlock jumper from the HVPS
2. Start up the system
3. Start running the treatment plan
4. Wait for 90 +/- 5 seconds after HVPS check
5. Check the system
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the high voltage interlock jumper is removed from the HVPS
2. Verify the system is started
3. Verify the running is started
4. Verify the 90 +/- 5 seconds passed after HVPS check
5. Verify system enters a fault state due to kV not reaching the target setpoint
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-14
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-101
TITLE: Operation 10 – Emission 3
STATEMENT: >>>
When user loads a firmware that reports a fault if the HVPS interface clamps the kV on emission.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. HVPS interface firmware which clamps the kV on emission
2. System is ready to run a treatment plan
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Load specialized HVPS interface firmware
2. Start up the system
3. Start running the treatment plan and emission
4. Check the emission
5. Check the fault
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the firmware is loaded
2. Verify the system is started
3. Verify the emission is started
4. Verify the emission did not complete successfully
5. Verify a fault is triggered for incomplete emission due to high voltage feedback
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-15
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-102
TITLE: Discharge 3
STATEMENT: >>>
Warm the system into "Ready" status and leave the system running without intervention for 2 minutes. Ensure that the system returns to cold state.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to use
2. The treatment plan is already loaded
3. Launch a timer to set the time
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Prepare button
2. Check the status of the system
3. Start the timer
4. Wait for 2 minutes
5. Check the status of the system
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the prepare button is clicked and the proper message is displaying in the GUI
2. Verify system switches to "Ready" status (check the top section of the monitor to find the status)
3. Verify the timer started
4. Verify 2 minutes passed
5. Verify system goes to COLD status
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-86
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-103
TITLE: Operation 09: Initiation
STATEMENT: >>>
When user runs a treatment plan and clicks the Beam-On button, the system enters Launching state first and then starts emission.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run
2. A treatment plan is loaded and ready to run an emission
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system
2. Load a treatment plan
3. Click the "Beam On" button
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is started
2. Verify a treatment plan is loaded successfully
3. Verify the system switches to Launching status and that the emission has not started yet
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-16
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-104
TITLE: Operation 08: Ready 1
STATEMENT: >>>
When user loads a plan with at least 6 operational points with alternating non-auto-execute and auto-execute points, verify user's intervention requirements.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run a treatment
2. A treatment plan is loaded into the system with at least 6 operational points with alternating non-auto-execute and auto-execute points
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run the loaded treatment plan with at least 6 operational points with alternating non-auto-execute and auto-execute points
2. Check the flags of the auto-execute points
3. Check the flags of the non-auto-execute points
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system started to run
2. Verify that the points which are flagged for auto-execute do not need user intervention to execute
3. Verify that the points which are flagged for non-auto-execute do need user intervention to execute
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-17
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-105
TITLE: Operation 08: Ready 2
STATEMENT: >>>
When user loads a plan with 1 operational point where the flag for auto-execute is set, verify user's intervention is required for running them.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run a treatment
2. A treatment plan is loaded into the system with 1 operational point with the flag for non-auto-execute
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run the loaded treatment plan with 1 operational point with the alternating non-auto-execute point
2. Check the flags of the loaded plan
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system started to run
2. Verify that despite being set to auto-execute, the point still requires user intervention to initiate emission (press "Beam On" button)
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-18
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-106
TITLE: Operation 07: Operational Point Setup 1
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user runs an emission with at least 2 points, verify that prior to emission of each point, the kV reading is within 5% of the target kV.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is up and ready to run an emission
2. A treatment plan is loaded and ready to run for at least 2 emissions
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system
2. Load the normal treatment plan with at least 2 points
3. Check the kV reading
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is started properly
2. Verify the plan is loaded
3. Verify that prior to emission of each point, the kV reading is within 5% of the target kV
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-19
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-107
TITLE: Operation 07: Operational Point Setup 2
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user runs an emission with at least 2 points, verify that prior to emission of each point, the kV reading is within 5% of the target kV.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is up and ready to run an emission
2. A treatment plan is loaded and ready to run for at least 2 emissions
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system
2. Load the normal treatment plan with at least 2 points
3. Check the kV reading
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is started properly
2. Verify the plan is loaded
3. Verify that prior to emission of each point, the kV reading is within 5% of the target kV
<<<
