[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-108
TITLE: Termination
STATEMENT: >>>
After finishing a treatment, the system needs to switch to STAGED status.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The treatment plan is loaded and the system is ready to run an emission
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the "Beam on" button
2. After the treatment is finished, check the status of the system
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission starts to run and the system switches to Emission status
2. Verify the status of the system is STAGED
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-85
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-109
TITLE: Operation 06 – HVPS Check
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user opens and closes the interlock door, verify FW can cycle HVPS interlocks successfully.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to run
2. The interlock door is open
3. A treatment plan is ready to load into the system
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Check the interlock door
2. Close the interlock door
3. Load and start to execute the treatment plan
4. Check the system status
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the door is open for a minimum of 1 second to force latched hardware interlock trigger without fault
2. Verify the interlock door is closed
3. Verify the treatment plan is loaded and running successfully
4. Verify that the system performs an HVPS check prior to ramping up high voltage and that the system is able to ramp up high voltage indicating that the interlocks have been cycled appropriately
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-21
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-110
TITLE: Operation 02: Warmup Procedure 1
STATEMENT: >>>
When user runs a specific invalid parameter warm up attempt, make sure it won't run and the system stays in COLD state and it will error in the logs.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is in COLD state
2. A treatment plan is loaded and ready to run
3. A specific version of invalid parameter warmup attempt is loaded in the system
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Load the invalid parameter warmup build in the system
2. Upload the treatment plan and check the system's state
3. Run Warm up
4. Click the Logs symbol
5. Check the logs
6. Check the system's state
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the build is loaded with invalid parameter warmup attempt
2. Verify it's in COLD state
3. Verify the warmup is started
4. Verify the logs are displayed in the screen
5. Verify the warmup was not successful
6. Verify the state of the system is COLD
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-22
  ROLE: Verifies

