[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-113
TITLE: Operation 4: Treatment Plan Confirmation 1
STATEMENT: >>>
When a special test is running for some of the points belonging to the treatment plan, then treatment of the loaded plan's execution never completes.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. A special test is ready for run which does not confirm all of the treatment plan's points
2. The treatment plan is loaded
3. System is ready to run a treatment plan
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run GUI with special test functionality to not confirm all points
2. Check running of the treatment plan
3. Check the logs
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the test is started to run
2. Verify running of treatment with multiple points won't complete
3. Verify logs indicate that treatment cannot be executed
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-24
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-114
TITLE: Operation 05: Treatment Plan Release 1
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user wants to run an emission with the interlock door is open, make sure FW can't run it.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is up and ready to run an emission
2. A treatment plan is loaded and ready to run an emission
3. Interlock door is open
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Check the interlock door
2. Try to run an emission for the loaded treatment plan by clicking the Beam on button
3. Click the Logs symbol in the left panel of the GUI
4. Check the logs
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the door is open
2. Verify the emission cannot be started because of the open door of interlock
3. Verify the logs are displayed in the middle of the screen
4. Verify the message for unsuccessful emission is displayed in the logs
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-25
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-115
TITLE: Operation 05: Treatment Plan Release 2
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user sends a request to attempt an invalid treatment plan, make sure the system can't progress to ramp high voltage and run an emission. A treatment plan request will be considered invalid if the system is not in the staged state with a confirmed treatment plan.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run
2. A treatment plan is ready for load in the system
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Load a GUI build which has functionality to attempt to release an invalid treatment plan which cannot be loaded and confirmed
2. Click the Logs symbol
3. Check the logs
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the build is loaded successfully
2. Verify the logs are displayed in the screen
3. Verify the unsuccessful attempt is displayed in the logs and the system cannot progress to ramp high voltage
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-26
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-116
TITLE: Operation 04: Treatment Plan Confirmation 3
STATEMENT: >>>
When user loads a plan with invalid treatment plan operational point confirmation parameters from the PC, the system should display an error. Incorrect parameters are values which do not match staged parameters.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run a treatment
2. A treatment plan is loaded into the system with incorrect parameters
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run the loaded treatment plan with invalid parameters
2. Click the Logs symbol in the left panel of the screen
3. In the logs, look for error messages
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system displays error messages for the invalid parameters and cannot pass the staged state
2. Verify logs are displayed in the middle of the screen
3. Verify the errors are related to invalid parameters of the loaded treatment plan
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-27
  ROLE: Verifies

