[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-118
TITLE: Operation 4: Treatment Plan Confirmation 2
STATEMENT: >>>
When user loads a plan with out of bound values, the system should display an error and record it in the logs. Acceptable values are: Acceleration potential (kV): 0–100 kV; Emission current (mA): 0–1 mA; Total delivery time: 0–300 seconds; Remaining delivery time: 0 to total delivery time; Beam optic focus adjustment values: 0–3 A.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run a treatment
2. A treatment plan is loaded into the system with invalid parameters
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run the loaded treatment plan with invalid parameters
2. Click the Logs symbol in the left panel of the screen
3. In the logs, look for error messages
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system displays error messages for the invalid parameters
2. Verify logs are displayed in the middle of the screen
3. Verify the errors are related to invalid parameters of the loaded treatment plan
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-29
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-119
TITLE: Operation 04: Treatment Plan Confirmation 6
STATEMENT: >>>
When user loads and runs a normal plan, make sure the parameters match with defined acceptable ranges: Acceleration potential (kV): 0–100 kV; Emission current (mA): 0–1 mA; Total delivery time: 0–300 seconds; Remaining delivery time: 0 to total delivery time; Beam optic focus adjustment values: 0–3 A; Beam optic deflection adjustment values: -1.5 A to +1.5 A; Filament current (mA): 0–3999 mA.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to use
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system
2. Load the normal treatment plan
3. Start running the loaded plan
4. Click Services in the left panel of the screen
5. Check the services
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is started properly
2. Verify the plan is loaded
3. Verify the running of the plan is started properly
4. Verify Services can be displayed in the GUI
5. Verify all of the parameters of the treatment plan can be found in the services matching the defined acceptable ranges
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-30
  ROLE: Verifies

