[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-123
TITLE: Fault Mode 2
STATEMENT: >>>
Firmware shall enter fault mode when a fault is detected.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready for use
2. A treatment plan is loaded and ready to run
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system
2. Wait till the state of the system changes to COLD
3. Push the e-stop button
4. Release the e-stop button
5. Reset the fault
6. Load a treatment plan
7. When the plan is in staged state, press the e-stop button
8. Check for system's mode
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is started
2. Verify the state of the system is COLD
3. Verify system induces a fault and the status displays a fault status in the GUI
4. Verify physically that the e-stop button is released
5. Verify the fault is reset
6. Verify the plan is loaded
7. Verify the state of the system as well as the pressing of the e-stop button
8. Verify fault is created and system enters fault mode
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-80
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-124
TITLE: Fault Information 3
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system enters fault mode after an e-stop event, it does not automatically exit fault mode when the e-stop is released.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is on and running
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. When the system is running, push the e-stop button
2. Click the Logs symbol in the left panel of the screen
3. Release the e-stop button
4. Monitor the system for 1 minute
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system induces a fault and the status displays a fault status in the GUI
2. Verify logs can be seen in the middle of the screen and the created fault is visible in the logs
3. Verify physically that the e-stop button is released
4. Verify the system does not exit from fault mode
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-79
  ROLE: Verifies

